1
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:11,550
Let's read lesson "Paper Cranes" together.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:26,040
America dropped two atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki,

3
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:36,530
taking lives of nearly half a million people.

4
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:47,040
When Hiroshima was bombed,

5
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:58,660
little Sadako was 2 years old and luckily escaped.

6
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:10,730
But she was exposed to radiation.

7
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:20,240
Ten years later, she fell seriously ill.

8
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:24,600
The girl believed in a legend saying

9
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:39,040
The girl believed in a legend saying if she folded enough 1000 paper cranes, she would recover.

10
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:47,880
She quietly folded cranes.

11
00:01:47,880 --> 00:02:00,680
Knowing this, children all over Japan and many places in the world sent thousands of cranes to Sadako.

12
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:13,910
But Sadako died when she had folded only 644 cranes.

13
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:44,310
Moved by her death, students in Hiroshima city raised money to build a monument to remember atomic bomb victims.

14
00:02:45,080 --> 00:03:00,880
On top of the 9-meter monument is a figure of a little girl raising both hands holding a crane.

15
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:06,170
Under the monument is engraved:

16
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:16,260
"We want this world to be forever peaceful."

